{
  "title": "Namaz on Friday Nights and the Night of Eid al-Adha for Fulfillment of Needs",
  "data": "Offer a two-unit prayer. In each unit, recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5), and when you reach the following verse, repeat it one hundred times:\nاِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَاِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِيْنُ\nIYYAAKA NA'BUDU WA IYYAAKA NASTA'EEN\nYou alone do we worship, and You alone do we ask for help.\nThen complete Surah al-Fatihah and recite [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) two hundred times.\nUpon accomplishment of the prayer, repeat the following seventy times:\nلَا حَوْلَ وَلَا قُوَّةَ اِلَّا بِاللّٰهِ الْعَلِيِّ الْعَظِيْمِ\nLAA HAWLA WA LAA QUWWATA ILLAA BILLAAHIL A'LIYYIL A'ZEEM\nThere is no might and no strength save in Allah, the High, the Great.\nThen prostrate and repeat the following two hundred times:\nيَا رَبِّ\nYAA RABB\nO my Lord!\nThen pray to Almighty Allah for whatever you want, and all your requests will be granted, Allah willing.",
  "merits": "Sayyid Ibn Tawus (r.a.) has reported this prayer for Friday nights and the night before the Day of Eid al-Adha (the tenth of Dhul Hijjah)."
}
